  "notes": "{嗅|か}ぐ means to smell or sniff—the active verb for perceiving odors.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{嗅|か}ぐ is transitive—you smell something:\n- ⟦{匂|にお}い→匂い：00874_nioi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{嗅|か}ぐ: to smell a scent\n- ⟦{香|かお}り→香り：00189_kaori⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{嗅|か}ぐ: to smell a fragrance\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {嗅|か}ぐ: to smell (active, intentional)\n- ⟦{匂|にお}う→匂う：00319_niou⟧: to smell, give off odor (intransitive)\n- ⟦{匂|にお}い→匂い：00874_nioi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: there is a smell\n\nONOMATOPOEIA:\n- ⟦くんくん→くんくん：noentry⟧{嗅|か}ぐ: to sniff around (like an animal)\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {嗅|か} combines the mouth and smell radicals.",
